                          %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
              \-colourability is a
              = succeed "." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  knot invariant
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/knot++invariant"} ?
          %p
            The proof is amusing to work out oneself. You have to show that if a knot diagram
            %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is
            = succeed "-colourable" do
              %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reidemeister+move"} Reidemeister move
            on it then the result is also
            = succeed "-colourable." do
              %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
          .un_note
            %h6#notes Notes
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  We can now use phrases such as ‘the trefoil knot is
                  = succeed "-colourable\u2019" do
                    %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
                  = succeed ".)" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reidemeister+moves"} Reidemeister's theorem
              %li
                %p
                  As the trefoil knot is
                  = succeed "-colourable" do
                    %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em non-trivial knots exist
                  = succeed "-colourable" do
                    %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
                  %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 8
                  is not, so these are different. We also get that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bridge+number"} bridge number
                  of the trefoil is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %p
            There are two comments to make here. First what does this all mean at a deeper topological level? The other is : why stop at
            = succeed "?" do
              %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            = succeed "-colourability?" do
              %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %h2#colourability_3
            %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-colourability
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            be an integer - in practice
            %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            or 2 are not that interesting, so usually
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 3
            %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_n
            be the additive group of integers modulo
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An
              %em
                %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-colouring
              of a knot diagram,
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_n
              in such a way that, at each crossing, the sum of the values assigned on the underpass arcs is twice that on the overpass, and such that in the assignment at least two elements of
              %math#mathml_97d871a90076ba9ee1a41044592d45e7c6b1d091_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_n
              are used.
          %svg#svg2{:height => "101.35714", :version => "1.0", :width => "89.928581", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"}
            %defs#defs4
              \&lt;inkscape:perspective id='perspective10' inkscape:persp3d-origin='372.04724 : 350.78739 : 1' inkscape:vp_x='0 : 526.18109 : 1' inkscape:vp_y='0 : 1000 : 0' inkscape:vp_z='744.09448 : 526.18109 : 1' sodipodi:type='inkscape:persp3d'&gt;&lt;/inkscape:perspective&gt;
            \&lt;sodipodi:namedview bordercolor='#666666' borderopacity='1.0' gridtolerance='10000' guidetolerance='10' id='base' inkscape:current-layer='layer1' inkscape:cx='47.132334' inkscape:cy='42.148486' inkscape:document-units='px' inkscape:pageopacity='0.0' inkscape:pageshadow='2' inkscape:window-height='701' inkscape:window-width='640' inkscape:window-x='0' inkscape:window-y='22' inkscape:zoom='2.8' objecttolerance='10' pagecolor='#ffffff' showgrid='false'&gt;&lt;/sodipodi:namedview&gt;
